OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Foreign Secretary Sir Geoffrey Howe
OL,6, has described Salman Rushdie's book,
OL,7, The Satanic Verses, as "offensive".
OL,9,FIn an implicitly conciliatory gesture
OL,10,Ftowards Iran, he said he understood why
OL,11,Fthe book had been criticised and said
OL,12,FBritain did not agree with its views.
OL,14,FBut Sir Geoffrey stressed that Britain
OL,15,Fcould not allow the principle of
OL,16,Ffreedom of speech to be overturned.
OL,18,FEarlier, Britain rejected an offer of
OL,19,Ftalks from Iran on the affair, saying
OL,20,FIran's threats of violence against
OL,21,FMr Rushdie must be lifted first.
OL,23,T]CFrom 02-03-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
