PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1772486495
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G3/9
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, EC environment ministers in Brussels
OL,6, have agreed on the total elimination of
OL,7, chemicals which harm the ozone layer.
OL,9,FA 50 per cent cut in chlorofluoro-
OL,10,Fcarbons (CFCs) by 1998 had already
OL,11,Fbeen agreed and ministers were expected
OL,12,Fto extend this to an 85 per cent cut.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FBut the EC ministers instead agreed in
OL,15,Fprincipal on a total ban on CFCs by the
OL,16,Fyear 2000 and an 85 per cent cut as
OL,17,Fsoon as possible.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FBritain's environment minister, Lord
OL,20,FCaithness, said it was very exciting
OL,21,Fprogress and a substantial advance.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 02-03-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,190,120,250,0,100
PN,18104
